  *      removing anything. Repair is hook.sh, under the firewall lock,
  *   3e. Warden outbound state (v3.1.2): says WHICH of the four reasons the
  *      syslog carries no REAPER-WARDEN-OUT lines, once per state change,
+ *   3f. filter-table completeness (2026-09-13, review R15): the chains only
+ *      filter_setting() declares are present in router mode - else the box
+ *      is running start_default_filter()'s boot skeleton (no port forwards,
+ *      no VPN server chains) and says so, with one restart_firewall per boot,
  *   4. the GDX skb_idx pool (OPT-IN, rwatch_gdx=1, default off): host local TCP
  *      rides the GDX accelerator (HTOA license), whose 8192-entry pool drains
  *      silently when the Runner loop wedges - the stock stack has NO watchdog or
@@ -463,6 +467,31 @@ static void rwatch_gen(void)
 	  "  echo \"$WOKEY\" > /tmp/rwatch_warden_out 2>/dev/null\n"
 	  "fi\n"
 	  "\n"
+	  /* 2026-09-13 (review R15 field data): an RT-BE88U ran for two weeks on
+	   * start_default_filter()'s boot skeleton because one line of
+	   * /tmp/filter_rules was refused and iptables-restore is atomic - and
+	   * nothing on the box said so. INPUT_ICMP and SECURITY are declared
+	   * unconditionally by filter_setting() and by nothing else, so their
+	   * absence in router mode after boot grace means the full table never
+	   * loaded. One restart_firewall per boot is the heal: the restore path
+	   * now skips a refused line itself, so a second attempt can succeed where
+	   * the first did not, and a deterministic refusal is not retried every
+	   * tick. Reported as FAIL (not CRIT): the LAN is untouched, the WAN is
+	   * still policy-DROP - what is missing is everything the operator asked
+	   * the firewall to let through. */
+	  "# 3f) the filter table is still the boot skeleton: the full ruleset never loaded\n"
+	  "if [ \"$UP\" -ge \"$HEALGRACE\" ] && [ \"$(_nv sw_mode)\" = 1 ] \\\n"
+	  "   && ! iptables -nL INPUT_ICMP >/dev/null 2>&1 && ! iptables -nL SECURITY >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n"
+	  "  FAIL=\"$FAIL filter-skeleton\"\n"
+	  "  if [ ! -f /tmp/rwatch_skel ]; then\n"
+	  "    logger -t rwatch \"the firewall filter table is the boot-time default only (INPUT_ICMP and SECURITY chains absent): the full ruleset never loaded, so port forwards, VPN server chains and the DoS guard are NOT in force - see the firewall: lines in syslog and /tmp/err_rules; requesting one restart_firewall\"\n"
+	  "    touch /tmp/rwatch_skel\n"
+	  "    service restart_firewall >/dev/null 2>&1\n"
+	  "  fi\n"
+	  "else\n"
+	  "  rm -f /tmp/rwatch_skel 2>/dev/null\n"
+	  "fi\n"
+	  "\n"
 	  "# 4) GDX host-TCP pool: 0 available = the silent accelerator-wedge\n"
 	  "#    signature. OPT-IN (rwatch_gdx=1): reads a kernel accelerator /proc\n"
 	  "#    surface every tick; default-off until skb_idx is field-proven non-\n"
